-- ═══ 432 Doctoral Scholarship of the University of Innsbruck ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Doctoral Scholarship of the University of Innsbruck', provider = 'University of Innsbruck', coverage_type = 'Partial Funding', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'Awarded in tranches (the fetched call is the 3rd tranche 2026): applications ran 24 August - 9 October 2026 via the student portal LFU:online and are now closed; funding decisions are expected in December 2026 (start between December 2026 and June 2027). The next call is expected in late 2026 / early 2027 - no single published deadline exists yet, so no deadline_date is recorded.', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["PhD"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All doctoral programmes at the University of Innsbruck (including members of doctoral colleges)"]$j$, eligible_countries = $j$["Doctoral students enrolled at the University of Innsbruck as regular students and registered for continuation, with a registered dissertation - no nationality restriction is published (the call expressly provides for applicants whose previous degrees were completed outside Innsbruck)"]$j$, min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The Doctoral Scholarship of the University of Innsbruck is the university's own stipend for its doctoral candidates: a monthly allowance of €1,150 for a maximum of 24 months, conceived as start-up, interim, bridge or final funding within a doctorate. The scholarship is fixed for six months at a time - each continuation follows an interim review based on a progress report confirmed by the dissertation supervisor - and the 24-month period may be interrupted at most twice, each interruption lasting no longer than six months (otherwise a new application is required). Eligible applicants are all doctoral students, including members of doctoral colleges, who are enrolled at the University of Innsbruck as regular students, are registered for continuation and have a registered dissertation; they must show excellent academic success (an excellent grade point average completed within the normal duration of study - minimum duration plus two tolerance semesters per study/section, with any exceeding of the minimum duration justified in the CV) or scientific achievements. Evaluation weighs the dissertation project description, the assessment of the diploma or master's thesis, the grade point average in the prior studies and scientific achievements such as publications, presentations and project proposals, and the university aims to award at least 50 per cent of the funding to women. Two conditions shape the funding period: no employment at the University of Innsbruck is permitted during the scholarship, and employment outside the university of more than 15 hours per week is prohibited and leads to immediate cancellation; publications and the dissertation must acknowledge the scholarship, and payment is made exclusively by SEPA transfer. The current call (3rd tranche 2026) accepted applications via LFU:online from 24 August to 9 October 2026, with decisions expected in December 2026 and funding starting between December 2026 and June 2027; the next call is expected in late 2026 or early 2027.$desc$, requirements = $req$Enrolment comes first - the online system only allows an application from doctoral students enrolled as regular students at the University of Innsbruck, registered for continuation, with the dissertation registered. Academic bar: excellent study success (excellent GPA within the minimum duration plus at most two tolerance semesters per study/section; overruns must be justified in the CV) or scientific achievements - the call recommends applying only with very good grades; a maximum of two resubmissions are possible, and applicants involved in the university's main research areas (research areas, platform and centres, doctoral colleges) or (co-)working on project proposals have priority at equal scientific quality. The application package (via LFU:online) is an 8-12 page description of the dissertation project, a half-page layperson abstract in German, a recommendation letter from the dissertation supervisor, CV and publication list, plus - for candidates whose undergraduate studies were not completed at Innsbruck - the graduation certificate and the degree certificates of all studies. During the award, six-monthly progress reports confirmed by the supervisor govern continuation; University of Innsbruck employment is prohibited and outside employment above 15 hours per week cancels the grant; the German version of the call prevails over the English one. No numeric GPA figure ('excellent') and no scholarship-level IELTS figure are published, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/research/research-funding/phd/doctoral-scholarship/', source_url = 'https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/research/research-funding/phd/doctoral-scholarship/', application_url = 'https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/lfuonline_postfach.home?typ_in=143', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-28 (cleanup pass 112) from the University of Innsbruck's official 'Doctoral scholarship from the University of Innsbruck' page fetched the same day (3rd tranche 2026: monthly allowance EUR 1,150 for a maximum of 24 months with six-monthly interim reviews via supervisor-confirmed progress reports and at most two interruptions of up to six months each; conceived as start-up/interim/bridge/final funding; eligible = doctoral students enrolled as regular students and registered for continuation with a registered dissertation, including doctoral-college members, showing excellent academic success within minimum duration plus two tolerance semesters or scientific achievements; at-least-50%-to-women funding aim; priority for main-research-area involvement or project-proposal work at equal quality; no University of Innsbruck employment during the award and no outside employment above 15 hours/week; publication acknowledgement and SEPA-only payment; application via LFU:online 24 August - 9 October 2026 for this tranche with documents 8-12-page project description, German lay abstract, supervisor recommendation, CV/publications and external-degree certificates; decisions expected December 2026, start December 2026 - June 2027; next call expected late 2026/early 2027; German version prevails). The previously stored URL (uibk.ac.at/forschung/foerderungen/doktoratsstipendien/) returns 404 - the scheme now lives under research funding / Early Career. Title corrected from the generic importer label 'Innsbruck University PhD Grants' to the official scheme name; the two predecessor programmes (young-researcher doctoral scholarships and doctoral-college excellence scholarships) were merged into this single scholarship on 15 March 2024 per the university's own announcement, so one record correctly represents the family. Award stored as 1150 EUR/'month'/'fixed' (the rate on the fetched current call; earlier calls paid EUR 1,070-1,120). deadline_date NULL/'not_published': the 2026 tranche window has closed and the next call date is only announced as late 2026/early 2027; status 'upcoming' ahead of that call. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. university_id intentionally remains NULL: no University of Innsbruck record exists in the universities table yet - create/backlink recorded as a future task. Source 2649 repointed from the bare uibk.ac.at domain to the live official page. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with a dead link and no terms read.$note$, award_amount = 1150, award_currency = 'EUR', award_period = 'month', award_basis = 'fixed', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Monthly stipend of €1,150 for up to 24 months (fixed in 6-month blocks after supervisor-confirmed progress reviews; up to two interruptions of max 6 months each) - a start-up/interim/bridge/final funding stipend during the doctorate', tuition_coverage = 'Not a tuition instrument: the scholarship is a living-cost stipend paid by SEPA transfer; it neither pays nor waives any tuition fee.', english_requirements = 'No scholarship-level IELTS figure (application documents include a German-language lay abstract; the German version of the call prevails).', required_documents = $j$["Description of the planned dissertation project, 8-12 pages (state of international research, objectives/hypotheses, originality/innovation, methodology, work and time planning, collaborations, ethical aspects, literature)", "Abstract of approx. half a page in German, understandable for laypersons", "Letter of recommendation from the dissertation supervisor", "Curriculum vitae and list of publications (justify any exceeding of the minimum study duration here)", "If undergraduate studies were not completed at the University of Innsbruck: graduation certificate and the certificates (diploma/bachelor's/master's) of all studies"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"round": "3rd tranche 2026", "application_window": "2026-08-24 to 2026-10-09", "decision": "2026-12", "start": "2026-12 to 2027-06", "status": "closed"}, {"pattern": "Tranche-based, several calls per year (2026 ran at least three): applications via LFU:online during each call's submission period, decisions about two months later; next call expected late 2026 / early 2027"}]$json$ WHERE id = 432;

-- ═══ 378 RETIRE (invented name / discontinued landscape) ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-28 (cleanup pass 112) as an invented-name directory row. The stored title, 'Vienna Doctoral Schools (Dok29) Funding Grant', and its subdomain dok29.univie.ac.at (dead; fetch fails) identify no current University of Vienna award: the Vienna Doctoral Schools are a federation of individual doctoral schools (law, historical/cultural studies, philosophy, social sciences, computer science, physics, chemistry, mathematics and others) rather than one funding grant, and no instrument named 'Dok29' appears on the university's official pages. The closest formerly central scheme, the uni:docs fellowship programme (three-year employed doctoral fellowships), is now described only in the past tense on the university's research-services pages and its official page returns 404 - it has been discontinued as a standalone call. Current funded doctorates at Vienna run through advertised PraeDoc positions and doctoral-school recruitment calls (the doctorate portal's own reconstruction page, fetched 2026-10-28, points applicants to 'Open PraeDoc positions' at careers.univie.ac.at, and school-level fellowships such as sowi:docs are announced inside a university-wide doctoral recruitment call) - i.e. employment vacancies and school-specific schemes, not the single 'funding grant' this record claims. Rewriting it into any one of those would invent a different identity, so the reliability-4 row is retired; individually verified Vienna doctoral schemes may be added in a future additions batch. Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 121 withdrawn; source 2672 (previously the bare univie.ac.at domain) repointed to the doctorate portal used for this determination.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 378;

-- ═══ 431 RETIRE (directory) ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-28 (cleanup pass 112) as a generic directory row. 'TU Wien Doctoral College Grants' names no single award: TU Wien's live Doctoral Colleges page (fetched 2026-10-28; the URL stored on this row returns 404) is a directory of the university's structured doctoral colleges - roughly twenty-five current colleges across TU Wien, industry-partnered, FWF-funded and other groupings (CO2Refinery, DC:{CD}, ENROL, LogiCS, SecInt, Water Resource Systems, TU-DX, VGSCO, Clusters of Excellence and more) plus a long list of completed ones. Each college is its own thematic consortium that recruits doctoral candidates into funded positions through its own advertisements and rules; there is no common 'doctoral college grant' with shared amounts, deadlines or eligibility that this record could be rewritten into, and TU Wien even notes that doctoral candidates may be organizationally assigned to a college without their position being funded by it. Presenting the directory as one scholarship would mislead applicants, so the reliability-4 row is retired; real, individually verified colleges or calls may be added later as separate records. Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 631 withdrawn; source 2633 (previously the bare tuwien.at domain) repointed to the official Doctoral Colleges directory page used for this determination.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 431;

